[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: A grid of various video clips, illustrating the vast amount of video content generated. A file explorer UI showing "No results :(" for a search query "Crowd celebrating!", highlighting the difficulty of searching traditional video files.
AUDIO: 'Every day, the world generates more video than humans can watch in a lifetime. And yet, for most organizations, most of that video remains unused. Not because they lack footage, because video has always been opaque.'

[00:12] [scene:problem]
VISUAL: A video player UI with various document icons (Attendance.xlsx, Report.docx, Database.mdf) overlaid, suggesting that video content is not easily searchable like other data types. A video player UI with multiple search queries ("Fan waving to the camera", "Presenter laughing during an interview", "Disturbances during the night", "A door creaking open during a tense scene") demonstrating the natural language search capability.
AUDIO: 'You can search a document, a spreadsheet, a database. But, you can\'t search a gesture, a sound, a reaction, a moment that has no name.'

[00:25] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A video player UI showing a football match with a search query "Show me every goal celebration where the crowd erupts." and multiple "GOAL" markers on a timeline.
AUDIO: 'Twelve Labs changes that. Our intelligence layer doesn\'t stop at file names, tags, or transcripts. Our models read the room, understanding every visual signal, every audio cue, every word in context simultaneously.'

[00:39] [scene:result]
VISUAL: The same football match video, now with "Video analysis: Complete", "Generating report: Complete", and "Creating editable timeline: Complete" messages, indicating successful processing. A security camera footage UI with a search query "Show me any after hour disturbances and write". The security camera footage showing "SUSPICIOUS ACTIVITY" highlighted on a timeline, with "Video analysis: Complete", "Creating editable timeline: Complete", and "Generating report: Complete" messages.
AUDIO: 'The way a person does, but at any scale. With Twelve Labs, video becomes structured intelligence. Queryable moments, automated summaries, generated chapters, actionable insights'

[00:52] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A news broadcast video with a search query "Find all the touchdowns in this game".
AUDIO: 'without anyone watching it manually. A sports team that once spent hours clipping, now does it in a query. A broadcaster can connect live moments to decades of archives.'

[01:06] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A video of people in a room with a search query "Generate a performance report on this video" and "Video analysis: Complete", "Generating report:." messages.
AUDIO: 'Developers and enterprises can add video understanding to products, workflows, and decision systems. And every video indexed makes the system smarter. Deploy through cloud APIs, Amazon'

[01:19] [scene:result]
VISUAL: On-screen text: "Searched 1193 hours of encrypted footage in 0.8s", highlighting performance. A screen displaying logos of various companies and organizations, indicating partnerships or customers.
AUDIO: 'Bedrock, or within your own infrastructure. Built for speed, scale, and security, so teams can move fast without giving up control. Trusted by leading organizations across sports, media, and'

[01:31] [scene:partners]
VISUAL: A screen displaying logos of various investors, indicating backing. A video player UI showing a dragon flying, with a timeline segmented into "Opening", "Rising Action", "Midpoint", and "Ending", demonstrating automated chapter generation.
AUDIO: 'enterprise. Backed by the investors building the foundation of modern AI infrastructure. Video has always contained everything. Now, you can use it.'

